'finalizer': ["When When combining proposals where one is a valid manipulation action for the current state and another is an invalid pick given the robot's location or gripper occupancy.: Select the proposal that is executable given the robot's current room and gripper contents; reject any pick that requires being in a different room or a free gripper that is not available.", 'When When combining proposals in a sequential manipulation task where proposals are redundant navigation commands that do not advance object transfer.: Prefer concrete manipulation actions (pick/drop) over repeated navigation; when the agent is at the source with free grippers, output a pick action rather than another move.', "When When combining proposals where some are 'think' statements and others are concrete actions.: When combining proposals, always choose the concrete executable action over any 'think' or meta-commentary statement, even if the latter is contextually correct, since only executable actions advance the goal and non-executable outputs waste steps and can cause failure."]}
